{"type":"message","id":"b45fb0b7","parentId":"0a281363","timestamp":"2026-01-31T14:42:58.254Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have enough data. Let me compile and write the report."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01FQcsaHv6bwgUH5ZBjz1Qx7","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/home/ec2-user/clawd/projects/sasha-job-search/reports/2026-01-31.md","content":"☀️ Sasha's Job Radar — January 31, 2026\n\nHey Sasha! Here's what's out there today 👀\n\n⚙️ Search Settings\n📄 Resume: Sasha_Greenspan_Resume_010326\n🔑 Keywords: Clinical Operations, Clinical Project Manager, Regulatory Specialist, Regulatory Affairs, Research Manager, Hospital Administration, Learning & Development\n📍 Remote (US) + Hybrid within 30mi of Baltimore\n💰 Minimum: $85k+\n\n📊 Today's Scan\n🔍 Scanned: 35+ companies + LinkedIn job boards | 🆕 New: 11 postings | ✅ Verified Live: 11 | ❌ Stale/Removed: 1 (UMB Sr. Director Clinical Business Operations — expired/redirected)\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🏢 **Johns Hopkins University** — Baltimore, MD\n\n1️⃣ Scientific Operations Officer (Neurology) 🔥🔥🔥\n💰 $99,800 – $175,000 | 📅 6 days ago\nDirector-level role overseeing scientific operations for neurology research programs. Manages teams, budgets, and cross-functional coordination. Strong fit for Sasha's research ops leadership background and PhD.\n🏷️ **Research Manager** · **Clinical Operations** · Neurology · **Team Leadership**\n🔗 [Apply on LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/scientific-operations-officer-neurology-at-the-johns-hopkins-university-4365703980)\n\n2️⃣ Director OHSR Operations (Office of Human Subjects Research) 🔥🔥🔥\n💰 $86,300 – $151,000 | 📅 ~2 weeks ago\nOversees operations for the Office of Human Subjects Research — IRB processes, regulatory compliance, research protections. This is basically Sasha's regulatory + research ops experience rolled into one dream role.\n🏷️ **Regulatory Specialist** · **IRB** · **Research Manager** · **GCP/ICH** · **Hospital Administration**\n🔗 [Apply on LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/director-ohsr-operations-office-of-human-subjects-research-at-the-johns-hopkins-university-4344893791)\n\n3️⃣ Clinical Research Site Manager (Neurology)\n💰 $55,800 – $97,600 | 📅 6 days ago\nManages clinical research site operations in neurology, including regulatory documentation, site coordination, and study conduct. Good match but salary range starts below $85K floor — upper end hits it.\n🏷️ **Clinical Operations** · **Regulatory Specialist** · **Research Manager** · Neurology\n🔗 [Apply on LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/clinical-research-site-manager-neurology-at-the-johns-hopkins-university-4365723094)\n\n4️⃣ Sr. Clinical Research Manager (Plastic & Reconstructive Surgery) 🔥\n💰 $64,600 – $113,300 | 📅 1 week ago\nSenior research management role overseeing clinical studies. Manages staff, regulatory submissions, data quality, and protocol compliance. Strong match for Sasha's clinical research management experience.\n🏷️ **Clinical Operations** · **Research Manager** · **Regulatory Specialist** · Surgery\n🔗 [Apply on LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/sr-clinical-research-manager-plastic-amp-reconstructive-surgery-at-inside-higher-ed-4365614444)\n\n5️⃣ Clinical Research Manager (Pulmonary)\n💰 $55,800 – $97,600 | 📅 4 days ago\nManages pulmonary clinical research operations including staff supervision, regulatory compliance, and data management. Similar to #3 — salary range straddles the floor.\n🏷️ **Clinical Operations** · **Research Manager** · Pulmonary\n🔗 [Apply on LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/clinical-research-manager-pulmonary-at-the-johns-hopkins-university-4366224640)\n\n6️⃣ Research Project Manager (Mental Health)\n💰 $55,800 – $97,600 | 📅 2 weeks ago\nProject management for mental health research programs. Coordinates multi-site studies, manages timelines and deliverables. Actively hiring.\n🏷️ **Research Manager** · **Clinical Operations** · Mental Health · Project Management\n🔗 [Apply on LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/research-project-manager-mental-health-at-the-johns-hopkins-university-4330499979)\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🏢 **Katalyst CRO** — Baltimore / Columbia, MD\n\n7️⃣ Senior Regulatory Affairs Manager (Columbia, MD) 🔥\n💰 Not listed | 📅 1 day ago\nSenior RA manager role at a CRO on Sasha's target company list. Manages regulatory submissions, strategy, and compliance for clinical trials. Contract position.\n🏷️ **Regulatory Affairs** · **Regulatory Specialist** · Clinical Trials · Pharma\n⚠️ CRO role — check if 5+ years CRO-specific experience required (dealbreaker)\n🔗 [Apply on LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/senior-regulatory-affairs-manager-at-katalyst-cro-4367400529)\n\n8️⃣ Sr. Regulatory Affairs Manager (Baltimore, MD) 🔥\n💰 Not listed | 📅 3 weeks ago\nSimilar senior RA role, Baltimore location. Also contract.\n🏷️ **Regulatory Affairs** · **Regulatory Specialist** · Clinical Trials\n⚠️ Same CRO experience caveat\n🔗 [Apply on LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/sr-regulatory-affairs-manager-at-katalyst-cro-4359791675)\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🏢 **University of Maryland, Baltimore (UMB)** — Baltimore, MD\n\n9️⃣ OPEN RANK: Project Manager or Senior Project Manager 🔥🔥\n💰 $105,000 – $135,000 | 📅 3 days ago\nOpen rank PM/Sr. PM position. Contract role. Strong salary range, well above floor. At a target university.\n🏷️ **Research Manager** · Project Management · **Clinical Operations**\n🔗 [Apply on LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/open-rank-project-manager-or-senior-project-manager-at-university-of-maryland-baltimore-umb-4366363753)\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🏢 **Nordberg Medical** — Baltimore, MD\n\n🔟 Regulatory Affairs Specialist US 🔥\n💰 Not listed | 📅 2 weeks ago\nMid-senior RA specialist for a biotech company on Sasha's target list. US regulatory submissions and compliance for medical devices.\n🏷️ **Regulatory Affairs** · **Regulatory Specialist** · Biotech · Medical Devices\n🔗 [Apply on LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/regulatory-affairs-specialist-us-at-nordberg-medical-4318546016)\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🏢 **Pace® Labs** — Maryland (Remote) 🏠\n\n1️⃣1️⃣ Senior Regulatory Affairs Specialist (Remote) 🔥🔥\n💰 $150,000 – $175,000 | 📅 2 days ago\nFully remote senior RA specialist. Excellent salary. Mid-senior level, regulatory strategy and submissions.\n🏷️ **Regulatory Affairs** · **Regulatory Specialist** · Remote · Labs\n🔗 [Apply on LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/senior-regulatory-affairs-specialist-remote-at-pace%C2%AE-labs-4314137229)\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🏢 **The Geneva Foundation** — Maryland\n\n📋 Clinical Data Manager\n💰 $75,000 – $95,000 | 📅 16 hours ago\nData management for clinical research — REDCap experience likely valuable. Geneva Foundation is on Sasha's target list. Salary starts below floor but upper end approaches it. Listed for awareness.\n🏷️ **Clinical Operations** · Data Management · **Research Manager**\n🔗 [Apply on LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/clinical-data-manager-at-the-geneva-foundation-4366232600)\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n⭐ **TOP PICKS** (strongest match + meets salary floor):\n\n1. 🥇 **JHU — Director OHSR Operations** ($86K–$151K) — IRB/regulatory ops leadership, tailor-made for Sasha\n2. 🥈 **JHU — Scientific Operations Officer, Neurology** ($99K–$175K) — Research ops + PhD-level leadership\n3. 🥉 **UMB — Open Rank PM/Sr. PM** ($105K–$135K) — Strong salary, target university\n4. 🏅 **Pace Labs — Sr. Regulatory Affairs Specialist** ($150K–$175K) — Remote, top salary, RA fit\n5. 🏅 **JHU — Sr. Clinical Research Manager** ($64K–$113K) — Upper range hits; strong clinical ops match\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n📉 Removed Since Yesterday\n- UMB Director, Senior Clinical Business Operations — listing expired/redirected\n\n📭 No new postings found from: Headlands Research, Pharmaron, Axon, AstraZeneca, Takeda, BeOne, FHI Clinical, Population Council, Emergent BioSolutions, Rho Inc, BioLink 360, CareFirst, McLaughlin Research Institute, EmVenio, Intralytix, Ascension, Kymera Therapeutics, Boeson Research, Alliance Clinical Network, Velocity Clinical Research, Vertex, Medtronic, Gilead Sciences, Philips, Regeneron, Amgen, Precision for Medicine, Paradigm Health, RTI International\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\nAll links LinkedIn-verified ✅ | Scanned 2026-01-31 ~14:40 UTC\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-opus-4-5","usage":{"input":1,"output":2822,"cacheRead":57004,"cacheWrite":3075,"totalTokens":62902,"cost":{"input":0.000005,"output":0.07055,"cacheRead":0.028502,"cacheWrite":0.01921875,"total":0.11827575000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1769870524321}}
